# Match guard as a callable function — the guard is invoked with the scrutinee.
# Previously this used block_on_anywhere(materialize(call_thunk)) in MatchGuardCheck,
# which caused nested async context issues. The iterative fix pushes a CEK continuation
# and returns Action::Materialize instead.
[
    positive?: [fn [let n] [> n 0]]

    result: [match 5
        x@[is: positive?]: "positive"
        _:                  "non-positive"]
]

---

%.result
=== out
String("positive")
